= 1 if the edge is kept, 0 otherwise; A(x, x) = 0.\n  Each value is noisy (between -1/(e^eps1 - 1) and e^eps1/(e^eps1 - 1)) but sums of A are unbiased counts.\n  A program reads either N(...) or A(...), not both; reading A costs the same budget as N.\n\nThis design round: do not use N(...). If the statistic needs edges between other nodes, read the unbiased matrix A(...); if it does not, use P only.\n\nThe input prompt from the analyst is:\n"""\nFor each node, the number of 2-stars centered at that node is the number of unordered pairs of its neighbors. This can be calculated as degree(node) * (degree(node) - 1) / 2, where degree(node) is the number of edges connected to the node. The total number of 2-stars in the graph is the sum of 2-stars centered at each node. Each node may hide its edge information under the local edge differential privacy framework. Q: The nodes are numbered from 0 to 48. What is the total number of 2-stars in the graph?\n"""\n\nThe graph has 49 nodes.\n\nBefore you answer, check the program line by line:\n1. no if, in, not in, <, >, == and no {...} or [...] anywhere;\n2. no **, // or %;\n3. every argument of comb, pow, + - * / is a number: size(S), never a set S;\n4. the only node names are self and the loop variables of sum(...);\n5. every name is assigned once and the last line is the return line.\n\nReply with exactly two parts after your reasoning:\n1. one code block that opens with the line ```dsl and closes with the line ```, holding only the program lines (no tags, no aggregate line inside the block);\n2. after the block, one line that starts with \'aggregate:\' followed by an arithmetic expression over total and n.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=13000, min_tokens=0, log